/-!
# Pair-free operational failure no-go in the existing revised-Q network

The revised-Q network has exactly two claim shapes: the inherited old claim
and the already generated M9 coface direction.  Every obstruction in that
network still denotes the inherited claim.  Consequently an
`ActualExpressibilityFailure` for a raw `Visible → Nat` language forces the
denotation of *every* raw program to be the old generated-direction claim.
That exclusion is fixed by the denotation before the later replay pair is
used; the pair cannot generate it.

The stronger K-faithful control below even lets an encoder choose an arbitrary
existing support and obstruction for every replay.  The later pair still
eliminates every such encoder because all those obstruction claims coincide.
Existing obstruction values are inhabited, so this is a carrier no-go rather
than an empty-source artifact.

If one pair-free raw intent denotes the actual obstruction claim,
failure is constructively empty for every inventory.  If every raw intent is
sent to the old generated direction instead, that direction is not the claim
of any existing obstruction.  A new `TheoryState` alone cannot change either
fact.  The missing upstream producer is therefore an event-generated
obstruction/claim coordinate carrying later-pair provenance; only afterward
may a new theory epoch audit it.  The existing relation, lineage and raw code
remain reusable dependent data, but the old M9 direction cannot be renamed as
the new residual.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

